# Enhanced Timetable Event Functionality

The current event creation is limited to a simple title prompt. I will implement a more robust system that allows users to specify duration, choose categories, and edit existing events.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend

#### [MODIFY] [main.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/timetable/main.py)
- **ADD**: `update_event` endpoint (`PUT /events/{event_id}`) to allow modifying existing events.
- **MODIFY**: [create_event](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/timetable/main.py#246-271) to ensure it handles all fields correctly (already seems okay, but will double-check).

### Frontend

#### [NEW] [EventModal.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/components/timetable/EventModal.tsx)
- Create a dedicated modal for creating and editing events.
- Features:
    - Title input.
    - Category selection (Study, Meeting, Personal, Deadline).
    - Start and End time selection.
    - Description (optional).
    - Delete button (if editing).

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/timetable/page.tsx)
- Replace simple [prompt](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/lib/uiStore.ts#79-99) in [handleCreateEvent](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/frontend/app/timetable/page.tsx#362-390) with the new `EventModal`.
- Add `handleEditEvent` function to open the modal for existing events.
- Update both grid views to trigger `handleEditEvent` when an event is clicked.
- Visual improvements:
    - Add category-specific icons (e.g., Book for Study, Users for Meeting).
    - Ensure colors are consistent with the category.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- I will use the browser subagent to:
    1. Navigate to `/timetable`.
    2. Click an empty slot to open the new `EventModal`.
    3. Create an event with a specific category and duration.
    4. Click the created event to open the edit modal.
    5. Update its title and duration.
    6. Verify the changes are reflected on the grid.
    7. Delete the event from the edit modal.

### Manual Verification
- User can test the flow of creating, editing, and deleting events with various categories and times.
